{
  "tab": "drop_tables",
  "note": "NOTE: drop_rate is a percent (25 = 25%, 0.5 = 0.5%). Each row is an independent roll. v0.1.2: every rate doubled after playtest (capped at 90%), relative rarity unchanged. Bands now: copper ~70%; category essences 40-60% (qty 1-3; bosses 80%, 2-5). Monster Essence ~30%; Training Scroll ~12%. Material bands: commons 30-40%; uncommons 2-6%; crystals / Holy Essence / Soul Shard / Log ~0.6-2%; Heartwood boss-only ~4-10%; gear ~0.1-0.4%; ultra-rares ~0.02-0.1%. Healing and MP drinks are NOT on every monster — only overlapping subsets of thematically related ones, at low rates. Quantities (min_qty-max_qty, rolled weighted toward the low end): copper 1-4, essences 1-3, Monster Essence 1-2, common materials 1-3, uncommon materials 1-2, rares/gear/consumables/junk 1. Mid curios and rare high-sell junk are shared by 2-3 related monsters. unlock_requirement_id is optional (e.g. unlock_cursed_dust). v0.1.2-gear: each monster has its own gear pool (class-specific Hide / Linen / Trail sets and mid weapons in Sunny Pasture). Gear quantity is always 1 (an instance with rolled stats); magic (~1/12) is rolled on the instance, not a separate row. v0.1.3: pasture gear is very rare (0.18–0.35% per entry; pool sums ≈1.05/1.50/1.87% for mouse/sheep/crow, ≈1.34% overall ≈ 1 piece per 75 kills, in the 60–100 target). Magic stays 1/12 of gear drops. Monster Essence 36% (1–2) on every mob, above category essence (16–20%, 1–2) so basic-skill fuel is more common and category essence feels earned. Nature/Elemental/Spirit qty capped at 1–2 (bosses 1–3 at 36–40%). Copper, common mats, scrolls, uncommons and rares were already in band and are left (see the v0.1.3 audit). v0.1.3b: pasture gear retargeted to ≈1 piece per 150–200 kills per mob pool (mouse 0.54% / 1 in 185, sheep 0.66% / 1 in 152, crow 0.63% / 1 in 159). Entries 0.06–0.18% (Crow’s 9-item pool has to sit slightly under 0.1% on some mid weapons). Magic stays 1/12 of a gear drop. Boar and Stump pools brought into the same band. v0.2.0: Dirt Banks materials (Dry Root, Tough Root) are shared across pasture and Banks, with better rates in the Banks. Warm Stone is sell-only junk on Ember Beetle / Earth Sprite / Frost Moth. Stone Club is a Warrior mid weapon (mole 0.24% + leather 0.32% = 0.56% pool; sprite 0.60% with cloth; crow 0.06% and hide cap/boots trimmed so the pool stays 0.67%). Ember Beetle first gear pool 0.62%. Cracked Bank Stone and Smoldering Scale are rare quest-start drops (questlines in a later milestone). All new gear pools follow the v0.1.3 1-per-150–200 rule; ME stays more common than category essence.  v0.2.3: Wild Apple drops removed. Field Mouse 6% Strawberry, Wool Sheep 6% Blueberry (was apple 4%). Wool-Shoulder guaranteed 5–15 Copper is handled in on-kill, not as a 100% drop-table row (so droprate bonuses cannot multiply it).  v0.2.3: copper drop chance raised for Crow (60→80) and Dirt Banks regulars (mole/sprite 60→80, ember beetle 64→82, spark bug 50→80). Quantity bands unchanged. Named quest bosses have no copper drop-table row (Wool-Shoulder’s 5–15 is a guaranteed on-kill).  v0.2.4: Spark Bug and Frost Moth retuned for the Dirt Banks — shared Dry Root / Tough Root / Earth Grit / Warm Stone, unique Spark Shell (2.4%) and Pale Wing (2.2%), warrior gear pools 0.56% / 0.62% (≈1 in 179 / 161). ME 36% stays above EE 18%. Frost Moth copper 80. Rogue/mage mid weapons trimmed so the 150–200 band holds.  v0.2.5: berries, Stone Chunk on Earth Sprite, ME/NE/scrolls/roots/Branch rates; Earth Shard on Burrow Mole for the Earthbreaker recipe.  v0.2.6: resource stacks ~1.5-2× larger; junk (Broken Twig, Torn Cloth, Lost Button, Pasture Bell, Cracked Shell) removed from every table; Smoldering Scale 20%/12%; Ice Shard on Spark Bug; named-rate bumps for Warm Grain, Earth Shard, Tough Root, Fire/Lightning Shard, Stone Chunk.",
  "columns": [
    "monster_id",
    "item_id",
    "drop_rate",
    "min_qty",
    "max_qty",
    "unlock_requirement_id"
  ],
